    "exhort": {
      "word": "EXHORT",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To incite by words or advice; to animate or urge by arguments, as to a good deed or laudable conduct; to address exhortation to; to urge strongly; hence, to advise, warn, or caution. Examples gross as earth exhort me. Shak. Let me exhort you to take care of yourself. J. D. Forbes.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To deliver exhortation; to use words or arguments to incite to good deeds. With many other words did he testify and exhort. Acts ii. 40.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "Exhortation. [Obs.] Pope.",
